      "problem": "Solve $f(x)=0,$ where $f(x) = \\dfrac{2x + 1}{x^2 + x - 6}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+1}{(x+3)(x-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =-1 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(x)=0$ is $x=-\\dfrac{1}{2}.$",
